# This repo is edited on Windows and run on a Raspberry Pi. Line endings are
# the single most common way to break it: a script checked out with CRLF makes
# bash read "set -euo pipefail\r" and die with
#
#     ./scripts/dev.sh: line 15: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# Force LF in the working tree regardless of core.autocrlf, so `git pull`,
# `scp` and hand-copied files all behave the same. Keep this file in sync with
# the editor settings; it is the safety net, not the primary fix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.apk binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
